    "created_at": "2026-02-10T23:48:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-10T23:48:03Z",
    "body": "I wrote the media-loading-state-timing.sub.html test for https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11959, but reading the spec I had completely missed that `:stalled` should only match when`:buffering` does, and only considered the \"is currently stalled\" state.\n\nSo that test needs to change.\n\nBut does the spec need to change? It looks to me like https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#selector-stalled matches [WebKit](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/9c8ea0e2de3976a4d051f63c27387bd3e3c236f4/Source/WebCore/html/HTMLMediaElement.cpp#L4888), including the `readyState` check.\n\nThe one thing that isn't exactly the same is that the spec updates the \"is currently stalled\" right before dispatching the \"stalled\" event, while WebKit's `m_sentStalledEvent` is set to true right after queuing a task to dispatch the event. So scripts could observe that `:stalled` matches before the \"stalled\" event, which is impossible per spec. But that timing issue isn't possible to write a non-flaky test for.\n\nI also looked at the other pseudo-classes in [WebKit source](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/9c8ea0e2de3976a4d051f63c27387bd3e3c236f4/Source/WebCore/css/SelectorCheckerTestFunctions.h#L487-L527) and can't find anything else that's different.\n\nSo, is the only action here to fix the test?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
